Liberating Scripture Collective — Licensing
============================================

This repository holds two kinds of material under two different licenses.

1. SOFTWARE — the website's source code (Astro components, layouts, scripts,
   styles, build tooling, configuration). Licensed under the MIT License
   (full text below). You may copy, modify, and reuse it freely, including
   for commercial purposes.

2. CONTENT — the organization's written copy (mission and project
   descriptions, page text, and similar prose), logos, photos, podcast
   artwork, and other creative or brand assets. All rights reserved. Unlike
   the SOFTWARE above, none of this content is available under MIT, Creative
   Commons, or any other public license — no permission is granted to copy,
   distribute, modify, or otherwise reuse it. For permission requests,
   contact https://liberatingscripture.org/contact/.

Which material is CONTENT (all rights reserved), not SOFTWARE:
  - Everything under public/assets/ (the org's logo, podcast cover art,
    screenshots, and Open Graph share images)
  - src/content/ (the /apps page's section copy, in markdown frontmatter
    and body text)
  - The site's written copy elsewhere. Most of it is embedded directly in
    the page templates under src/pages/ and src/components/ rather than
    kept in separate content files — in those files, the HTML structure,
    CSS classes, and logic are SOFTWARE (MIT), but the actual prose
    (headings, body text, meta descriptions, and similar wording) is
    CONTENT and is NOT covered by the MIT grant below, even though it
    lives in the same file.

Everything else — the Astro components, layouts, scripts, styles,
configuration, and build tooling, apart from the embedded prose described
above — is SOFTWARE under the MIT License.

